@participant3 to clarify, is the above crash from your application or from a sample electron app ? If it is from your application, add the feature flag to this callsite https://github.com/signalapp/Signal-Desktop/blob/4d2910d696fc22fd74dd36c3fa3749fb855e184a/app/main.ts#L1677

```
app.commandLine.appendSwitch('disable-features', 'HardwareMediaKeyHandling,PartitionAllocBackupRefPtr');
```

@participant2 Ah thank you for the tip on how to use the feature flag correctly! However, after following the steps I'm still getting the same crash and stacktrace in `electron!partition_alloc::internal::PartitionBucket::MaintainActiveList()`.

To confirm the flag was passed to electron I used `ps aux` and observed electron was running with ` --disable-features=HardwareMediaKeyHandling,PartitionAllocBackupRefPtr,SpareRendererForSitePerProcess`.

Regarding the other flag `--enable-features=PartitionAllocBackupRefPtr:brp-mode/enabled` I wasn't sure how to use it. When adding `app.commandLine.appendSwitch('enable-features', 'PartitionAllocBackupRefPtr:brp-mode/enabled')` the switch seems to be discarded as observed with `ps aux`. (But using just `'enable-features', 'PartitionAllocBackupRefPtr` works correctly.)

@participant1 to confirm, did you add `PartitionAllocMemoryReclaimer` to the `--disable-features` command line flag similar to https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/39775#issuecomment-1714945631 after the backport ?

> Given that it seems that everyone is able to reproduce it, do you need any further action from us?

I tried to repro with the gists from https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/39515 which also share the same stack trace and was not able to confirm the crash in Fedora 36 arm64 vm and Ubuntu 22.04 x86_64 vm. Both vm use 4k page size if that makes any difference. Additionally, there are reports of the crash being addressed with v27 beta, if possible please check if that is the case for your application as well.

@participant1 given you are able to crash consistently on fedora, can you share the steps that I can try. Thanks!

@participant2 ah, I just found out how to use custom Electron builds in Fiddle. I'm happy to test it! However: How do I get a crashpad dump in Fiddle? I tried the following:

```ts
crashReporter.start({
  submitURL: 'https://example.invalid/crash-report',
  uploadToServer: false,
});

...

app.whenReady().then(() => {
  app.setPath('crashDumps', '/tmp/crashes');
});
```

...but no crash dumps are generated.

Or should I simply attach the regular sytemd coredump instead?
